##
#
# Thacker's planar surface flow in a paraboloid-shaped basin [3], Section
# 5.3.2
# (Table 5) of [1], in the configuration of Delestre et al. [2, Sec.
# 4.2.2].
#
# A planar free surface rotates periodically in the radially symmetric
# basin
#
#   z(x) = -h_0 (1 - |x - x_c|^2 / a^2)
#
# with h_0 = 0.1 m, a = 1 m, eta = 0.5, center x_c = (2, 2) and g = 9.81,
# without friction. The moving shoreline is circular at all times. The
# computational domain is [0,4]^2. The final time is three periods of the
# motion,
#
#   T = 3 * 2 pi / sqrt(2 g h_0) = 13.4571044 s.
#
# We report the normalized L1, L2, and Linf errors of the water depth h at
# final time.
#
# While the paper states slip boundary conditions, the domain boundary
# stays dry for all times, and with "do nothing" conditions (used here) the
# errors of Table 5 are reproduced to three digits.
#
# The chosen refinement level 6 corresponds to 4225 Q1 degrees of freedom
# (second row of Table 5 of [1]). Table 5 is obtained with mesh refinement
# 5 to 10 (1089 to 1050625 dofs), with RK(3,3;1) (erk 33) and RK(3,3;1/3)
# (ssprk 33) at CFL 0.5.
#
# [1] J.-L. Guermond, M. Maier, E. J. Tovar. A high-order explicit
#     Runge-Kutta approximation technique for the shallow water equations.
#     Comput. Fluids, 288:106493, 2025. DOI 10.1016/j.compfluid.2024.106493,
#     arXiv:2403.17123
#
# [2] O. Delestre, C. Lucas, P.-A. Ksinant, F. Darboux, C. Laguerre,
#     T. N. T. Vo, F. James, S. Cordier. SWASHES: a compilation of shallow
#     water analytic solutions for hydraulic and environmental studies. Int.
#     J. Numer. Methods Fluids, 72(3):269-300, 2013. DOI 10.1002/fld.3741
#
# [3] W. C. Thacker. Some exact solutions to the nonlinear shallow-water
#     wave equations. J. Fluid Mech., 107:499-508, 1981.
#     DOI 10.1017/S0022112081001882
#
##

subsection A - Scheduler
  set basename          = paraboloid

  set tasks             = error evaluation

  set final time        = 13.45710440
  set timer granularity = 13.45710440
end


subsection B - Equation
  set dimension                    = 2
  set equation                     = shallow water

  set gravity                      = 9.81
  set manning friction coefficient = 0

  set reference water depth        = 0.1
  set dry state relaxation small   = 1e2
  set dry state relaxation large   = 1e4
end


subsection C - Discretization
  set geometry            = rectangular domain
  set mesh refinement     = 6

  subsection rectangular domain
    set boundary condition bottom = do nothing
    set boundary condition left   = do nothing
    set boundary condition right  = do nothing
    set boundary condition top    = do nothing

    set position bottom left      = 0, 0
    set position top right        = 4, 4
  end
end


subsection E - InitialValues
  set configuration = paraboloid
  set position      = 2, 2
  set direction     = 1, 0

  subsection paraboloid
    set eta                 = 0.5
    set free surface radius = 1
    set water height        = 0.1
  end
end


subsection H - TimeIntegrator
  set cfl min               = 0.50
  set cfl max               = 0.50
  set cfl recovery strategy = none
  set time stepping scheme  = erk 33
end


subsection K - ErrorEvaluation
  set error normalize  = true
  set error quantities = h
end
